[2m2026-08-20T06:52:10.838949Z[0m [33m WARN[0m [2mda::load_journey[0m[2m:[0m [3marticle_id[0m[2m=[0m"2606.11173" [3martifact_id[0m[2m=[0mFigure3 [3mreason[0m[2m=[0mno section contains the figure caption "Figure 3 Fully-correct rollout. Per-token advantages 𝐴SD𝑡 ( ?\u{302}?𝑡) (see Eq. 4) along a single student trajectory that reaches the correct boxed answer. StepAlignFB (top) produces positive advantages throughout the trace, reinforcing the student’s correct reasoning trace. RefSol (bottom) produces diffuse negative advantages across the entire rollout: the teacher prefers the alternative derivation’s surface form even though the student’s answer is correct, mixing stylistic disagreement into the gradient." [3mevent[0m[2m=[0m"da_load_journey_figure_grounding_skipped"
[2m2026-08-20T06:52:10.839266Z[0m [33m WARN[0m [2mda::load_journey[0m[2m:[0m [3marticle_id[0m[2m=[0m"2606.11173" [3martifact_id[0m[2m=[0mFigure4 [3mreason[0m[2m=[0mno section contains the figure caption "Figure 4 Incorrect step. Per-token advantages for a rollout containing an error at the step marked by the dashed line. StepAlignFB (top) produces a sharp negative shift at the tokens after the erroneous step, while reinforcing correct reasoning in the preceding steps. RefSol (bottom) produces broadly negative advantages across the entire trace, conflating the error with everywhere the student’s path diverges from the canonical solution." [3mevent[0m[2m=[0m"da_load_journey_figure_grounding_skipped"
[2m2026-08-20T06:52:10.839504Z[0m [33m WARN[0m [2mda::load_journey[0m[2m:[0m [3marticle_id[0m[2m=[0m"2606.11173" [3martifact_id[0m[2m=[0mFigure5 [3mreason[0m[2m=[0mno section contains the figure caption "Figure 5 Incomplete solution. Per-token advantages for a rollout that exhausted the token budget without producing a final answer. The student’s reasoning trace is unpromising from the start and quickly devolves into guessing values for the variable before running out of budget. The critic responds by producing a complete alternative solution, yielding update signals similar to those of the reference solution." [3mevent[0m[2m=[0m"da_load_journey_figure_grounding_skipped"
[2m2026-08-20T06:52:10.840098Z[0m [33m WARN[0m [2mda::load_journey[0m[2m:[0m [3marticle_id[0m[2m=[0m"2606.11173" [3martifact_id[0m[2m=[0mFigure6 [3mreason[0m[2m=[0mno section contains the figure caption "Figure 6 Full verbatim repetition with appended correction. The critic includes the student’s incorrect step verbatim and follows it with a textual correction. Induction-head copying of the original (incorrect) tokens dominates the teacher’s distribution; per-token advantages are overwhelmingly positive." [3mevent[0m[2m=[0m"da_load_journey_figure_grounding_skipped"
[2m2026-08-20T06:52:10.840480Z[0m [33m WARN[0m [2mda::load_journey[0m[2m:[0m [3marticle_id[0m[2m=[0m"2606.11173" [3martifact_id[0m[2m=[0mFigure7 [3mreason[0m[2m=[0mno section contains the figure caption "Figure 7 Solution omitted from the teacher context. For a fully correct student solution, the critic acknowledges correctness without reproducing the trace. With no in-context anchor on the student’s tokens, the teacher’s distribution drifts toward alternative surface forms, producing negative advantages across the correct trajectory." [3mevent[0m[2m=[0m"da_load_journey_figure_grounding_skipped"
[2m2026-08-20T06:52:10.840810Z[0m [33m WARN[0m [2mda::load_journey[0m[2m:[0m [3marticle_id[0m[2m=[0m"2606.11173" [3martifact_id[0m[2m=[0mFigure8 [3mreason[0m[2m=[0mno section contains the figure caption "Figure 8 Solver prompt. The solver sees only the problem statement, with the same step-formatted instruction used by the evaluation harness so that on-policy training and inference share a prompt template." [3mevent[0m[2m=[0m"da_load_journey_figure_grounding_skipped"
